IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P4-gate: the two gates and the one month helper that the P4 modules share.
-- It restates no date of Article 111 or Article 113: it calls the keel's applicability function
-- (`Art 113 the provision group applies`) with the group the provision belongs to.
-- Articles 28 to 39 are in the group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78`
-- (applies from 2 August 2025, in both versions of the text; PLAN.md section 3).
-- Annex VII is given effect by Article 43 (Chapter III Section 5), so it is in the group `General`
-- (assumed, not ruled: PLAN.md section 3, "An Annex takes the group of the Article that gives it effect").
-- Annex XIV is given effect by Article 30(2), so it is in the group of Articles 28 to 39.
-- A result of NOTHING before the group applies is the keel's rule (BRIEF, "Application"): never JUST FALSE.

§ `The group of Articles 28 to 39 (and Annex XIV) on the date asked`

-- A question that is not about one AI system passes the core's two constants and FALSE (PLAN.md section 7), so
-- Article 111(2) saves nothing for this group: it speaks of operators of high-risk AI systems placed on the market earlier.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

-- The answer of a function of Articles 28 to 39, once the group applies; NOTHING before it applies.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the answer if the group applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` MEANS
    IF `Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST `the answer if the group applies`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113 third paragraph point (b) gives Chapter III Section 4 a date of application (2 August 2025)

-- The same, for a function whose own answer can be NOTHING.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the answer if the group applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 28 to 39 the maybe-answer when the group applies` MEANS
    IF `Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN `the answer if the group applies`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113 third paragraph point (b) gives Chapter III Section 4 a date of application (2 August 2025)

§ `The group of Annex VII on the date asked, for one AI system`

-- Annex VII is the conformity assessment procedure of Article 43 for a high-risk AI system. Chapter III Section 5 is in the
-- group `General`; Article 111(2) can save a high-risk AI system placed on the market earlier and not significantly changed.
-- A system that is not high-risk (`Route neither`) is outside Article 43 and so outside Annex VII.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Annex VII the group of Article 43 applies to the AI system on the date asked` MEANS
        `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
    AND (CONSIDER `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
         WHEN `Route neither` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- Article 2(2) (the keel's `aia-scope.l4`): for a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with products covered by the legislation of Section B of
-- Annex I, only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 apply (Articles 6(1), 102 to 109 and 112 as enacted). Article 43, which gives Annex VII
-- effect, is not among them. The keel's function answers JUST FALSE for Article 43 on such a system and NOTHING when it does not speak.
-- Annex VII is a procedure for one high-risk AI system, so every function and rule of `P4-annex-vii.l4` takes the keel's two further inputs
-- (the Section B flag and the integration flag) and asks the keel about Article 43 (fork F-S14-reach: assumed, not ruled; Articles 28 to 39
-- and Annex XIV concern notifying authorities and notified bodies, not a high-risk AI system as such, and do not ask).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Annex VII Article 2(2) cuts Article 43 off from the AI system` MEANS
    `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` (`Article reference` WITH number IS 43, letter IS "", paragraph IS 0) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The answer of a function of Annex VII, once the group applies; NOTHING before it applies or where the group does not reach the system.
-- Where the keel's Article 2(2) answers JUST FALSE for Article 43 the answer is JUST FALSE (PLAN.md seam S14: a flat "only ... shall apply").
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer if the group applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex VII the answer when the group applies` MEANS
    IF `Annex VII the group of Article 43 applies to the AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
    THEN IF `Annex VII Article 2(2) cuts Article 43 off from the AI system` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (a flat "only"; Article 43 is not on the list; fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE JUST `the answer if the group applies`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 43 (Chapter III Section 5, group General) gives Annex VII effect from the general date, for a high-risk AI system, and Article 111(2) saves a high-risk system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- The same, for a function whose own answer can be NOTHING.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer if the group applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex VII the maybe-answer when the group applies` MEANS
    IF `Annex VII the group of Article 43 applies to the AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
    THEN IF `Annex VII Article 2(2) cuts Article 43 off from the AI system` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (a flat "only"; Article 43 is not on the list; fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE `the answer if the group applies`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 43 (Chapter III Section 5, group General) gives Annex VII effect from the general date, for a high-risk AI system, and Article 111(2) saves a high-risk system placed earlier and not significantly changed

§ `Periods counted in months`

-- The text counts several periods in months (Article 30(4), 36(3), 36(7)(b), 36(8)(a), 36(9)). It does not say how a month is counted
-- (Regulation (EEC, Euratom) No 1182/71 does, and is not among the sources): the encoding takes the same day of the later month, and
-- the last day of that month where it has no such day (`add months` of the `daydate` library clamps). Assumed, not ruled (fork F-months).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
      `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 28 to 39 the date the number of months after` MEANS
    `add months` `the start` `the number of months`
